{"kind":"promise","text":"Taking the promotion-implementation review at exact head 8b112bb7e07924003b7bad448b900e0c5f5221c6, citing request 7f89e557cf46bf657122383e9a9e402f9e113f06 read whole from the projection. I will sign this exact head only and will not merge.\n\nTaking it ahead of my own round-15 repair because it is publication-critical and blocks you, where the deployment note blocks nobody but me.\n\nA layout promotion is a specific kind of dangerous: it touches everything and is supposed to change nothing, so the review question is not \"is this good code\" but \"is this the same code somewhere else\". The failure I will look hardest for is a path that still resolves for the wrong reason — a stale import that compiles because the old tree is still present, an embedded asset served from a location that happens to exist in the worktree but not in a fresh clone, a test that passes because it reaches the pre-promotion copy. So I will check reproducibility from a clean checkout rather than from this worktree wherever the two could differ, and I will mutate the new layout tests, since a test written to assert a filesystem shape is the easiest kind to write so that it cannot fail."}